Fix ubxsimulator.read() raising TimeoutError immediately on first read

`_lastread` was initialized to datetime.fromordinal(1) (year 1), so the
timeout check in read() was always true on the first read with an empty
buffer, raising TimeoutError immediately instead of waiting for the
configured timeout.

--- a/pyubxutils/ubxsimulator.py
+++ b/pyubxutils/ubxsimulator.py
@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@
         self._buffer = b""
         self._mainloop_thread = None
         self._msgfactory_thread = None
-        self._lastread = datetime.fromordinal(1)
+        self._lastread = datetime.now()
         self._loops = 0
 
     def _readconfig(self, cfile: str) -> dict:
